REM >TestDashMulti
REM Draw module test: Draw_Stroke with a 4-element dash pattern (two
REM different on/off widths, alternating: long-on, short-off, short-on,
REM long-off) and a nonzero pattern "start" offset, on a single long
REM line. TestDash only exercised a simple 2-element on/off pattern
REM starting at 0 - this checks dash() correctly cycles through more than
REM one on/off pair and honours a mid-pattern starting phase.
ON ERROR ERROR EXT ERR, REPORT$ + " at line " + STR$(ERL/10)

MODE "X640 Y480 C256"
SYS "ColourTrans_SetGCOL", &FFFFFF00,,,128,0
CLG
SYS "ColourTrans_SetGCOL", &800080FF,,,0,0

DIM path% 64
DIM trfm% 24
trfm%!0 = (1<<16) : trfm%!4 = 0
trfm%!8 = 0        : trfm%!12 = (1<<16)
trfm%!16 = 0        : trfm%!20 = 0

DIM lstyle% 16
!lstyle% = 0        : REM mitred join, butt caps
lstyle%!4 = &40000   : REM mitre limit 4.0 (16.16)
lstyle%!8 = 0
lstyle%!12 = 0

DIM dashpat% 32
!dashpat% = 1200     : REM start - a phase offset into the pattern below
dashpat%!4 = 4        : REM element_count
dashpat%!8 = 2400      : REM on  (long)
dashpat%!12 = 800      : REM off (short)
dashpat%!16 = 800      : REM on  (short)
dashpat%!20 = 2400      : REM off (long)

p% = path%
!p% = 2 : p%!4 = &1000 : p%!8 = &8000
p% += 12
!p% = 8 : p%!4 = &1F000 : p%!8 = &8000
p% += 12
!p% = 0 : p%!4 = 0

REM Thickness kept well above 2 OS units (512 in Draw units) - below that,
REM the reference module drops a dashed stroke entirely (see AGENTS.md);
REM this test isolates dash()'s multi-element/start-offset handling, not
REM that separate thin-line behaviour.
SYS "Draw_Stroke", path%, &30, trfm%, 256, 1500, lstyle%, dashpat%

*ScreenSave -native screen
